Debith's direction (2026-09-12, settled 2026-09-13): during work, memories record what was learned, concretely and with the case. When the user asks for a consolidation — at any point, not only at a session's end — the agent reads back what the session wrote and states once, at the level the cases support, a pattern several of them share. Design: overview §4.11, section 04 §3.9, section 00a Feature 7, section 01 §4, §7 and §8.

Built (2026-09-13): `remember` takes `generalises` — two or more heads, which stay heads and count as read; the service refuses one case, a non-head, an instance also superseded by the same write, and a generalisation that does not cover its instances on every hard dimension (a dimension's `any` covers everything, so overreach is caught in review). `review(session)` lists a session's writes with what already generalises each. The MCP server serves the steps as the `consolidate` prompt, started by the user.

Retrieval folds (Debith chose it over placing both): a candidate whose generalisation is also a candidate is named under it as `evidence` — key and title, no text, no budget — decided before scoring, so it depends on neither rank nor budget. The procedure slot never folds; a retired generalisation unfolds its instances. Trade-off accepted: a case may carry a detail the pattern dropped, and the reader must `show` it.

Still open (overview §10): what a later contradicting case should trigger.